  "encounterTable": "route_5",
  "_design": "Four shelves down into the volcanic interior, and the whole point of the map is that the GROUND changes along the road rather than at a door. The player leaves Tideglass on turf and gold dirt; nine rows later the turf is in patches, the road is black clinker, and the trees are dead standing. Nothing announces it. The three basalt bands are columnar rather than stratified, which is the one visual difference that stops this reading as the quarry two acts back.",
  "_plan": "The road coils: east along the top shelf, south down the eastern wall, west across the middle, south past the Coil, east along the Cinderfall, south to the gate. That is six legs and it doubles back on itself twice, so the Coil is seen from three sides before it is walked past. The optional branch is the steam terraces on the west, which rejoin the road lower down rather than dead-ending; the pool at the back of them is too deep to wade and is the reason to come back. Meridian have stopped moving and started digging: two fenced sites, numbered trenches, spoil graded and stacked, a generator running with nobody near it. Nobody on the map explains any of it.",
